# The linear residue of MUTABLE images created without a format list, per base format.
# Generated 2026-11-21 by `python3 scripts/nolist-residue.py results/raw/game-patched-imginv5.log`
#   (re-run that command to reproduce every number below).
#
# Input: results/raw/game-patched-imginv5.log (976648 B, sha256 80d433927103ef02...), the TU_IMG_INV=1
#   inventory of the RE4 game run on the ship stack `0001..0014` (p14 form of 0014 included, build
#   050375a18b7b as recorded in results/imginv-3variants.txt). `vkfmt=`/`fmt=` in that log are both
#   pipe-level names: exp-14's inventory prints util_format_name() twice (base layout format and the
#   create format converted through vk_format_to_pipe_format), so the Vulkan enum itself is not in the
#   log. That is enough here: the R- and B-spelled Vulkan formats of a pair are different pipe formats
#   (PIPE_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_* vs PIPE_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_*, PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10A2_UNORM vs
#   PIPE_FORMAT_B10G10B10A2_UNORM), and the one pipe format in this table with a single Vulkan spelling
#   is PIPE_FORMAT_R11G11B10_FLOAT, which only VK_FORMAT_B10G11R11_UFLOAT_PACK32 maps to.
#
# What this table is for: it sizes the residue that a wider no-list tiling rule would have to move -
# the largest number any such rule could ever be worth. It does not say whether moving them is legal:
# journal 39 answers that half (it is not - the Vulkan compatibility class of every one of these bases
# contains a member the A740 tiled path cannot express, `python3 scripts/class-order-check.py`).
#
# Split of the residue, from the same log (journal 39.3):
#   971 creates / 1630.2 MiB  16-bit- and 32-bit-class bases: linear because their own class contains a
#                             member the tiled store cannot express. The only part a rule could argue
#                             about, and closed by the spec's own class rule.
#    53 creates /   0.65 MiB  BC, 64-bit and 8-bit bases whose class scripts/class-order-check.py
#                             reports homogeneous. All 53 are in the `small` column: level 0 below the
#                             driver's width0 < 16 * blockwidth fallback (fd6_layout.c:155-161), a stock
#                             rule that fires for every image shape, list or no list.
#   In total 84 of the 1024 residue creates (0.9 MiB) are `small`; the other 31 of them are also
#   class-required linear, so nothing here is a rule that a layout patch could re-argue.
#
# MUTABLE_FORMAT is create-flag bit 0x8 (include/vulkan/vulkan_core.h:2764 at 6dfa32a); usage bits are
# SAMPLED 0x4, STORAGE 0x8, TRANSFER_SRC 0x1, TRANSFER_DST 0x2.

  (results/raw/game-patched-imginv5.log: 1 inventory lines cut by foreign stderr, not counted)
